#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bale — Claude session orchestrator.

v0.0.10. Hand-written, pre-tarball-protocol. Tracking incrementally
toward the v0.1 contract: apply.sh handling and post-apply manifest
reconciliation (BALE.md §11 rule 18) landed in v0.0.2; pack threshold
caps (BALE.md §7.4) and the --force override landed in v0.0.3; CODE.md
was added as a fourth global doc in v0.0.4, with the injection list,
install layout, and self-check scripts updated to match. The
configurables loader/merger and the `bale config init` wizard were
extracted from this file into the sibling `bale_config.py` module in
v0.0.4 to apply CODE.md §4.2 to the largest two sections; this file
now hosts the pack/apply/revert/retry/unlock/handoff pipelines, the
hook runtime, and the CLI surface. `bale unlock` (BALE.md §9.3) landed
in v0.0.5. `bale handoff` plus apply-time branching on
`response_kind: "bailout"` (TARBALL.md §5.6.3) landed in v0.0.6.
v0.0.7 finishes two follow-ups: `bale handoff` now pre-packs source
files extracted from handoff.md's `## Reading plan for the next
session` section (so the next request lands with the files Claude
recommended already in context/, instead of just handoff.md), and the
apply walkthrough's `[r]` revert action — previously a v0.1 stub that
told the user to run `bale revert <sid>` themselves — is wired
through to _discard_hold_state + clear_lock so the action completes
inline. v0.0.8 lands the BALE.md §10 git-init walkthrough: `bale pack`
in a non-git directory now offers to initialize the repo, prompts for
missing git identity (via bale_config.walkthrough_git_identity),
writes a .gitignore with the §6.4 baked-in exclusion set, and records
an initial commit before continuing into the rest of the pack
pipeline. v0.0.9 lands two coupled BALE.md §7.3 items: the
interactive pack wizard (`bale pack` with goal or --slug missing now
prompts on a TTY for the missing fields, plus constraints,
out_of_scope, and an optional README) and $EDITOR integration for the
README step. The editor invocation that `bale handoff --edit-goal`
introduced in v0.0.7 was generalized into a shared `open_in_editor`
helper so the pack wizard's README step and the handoff goal-edit
share one implementation. v0.0.10 lands the final BALE.md §7.3/§7.4
items: `.baleignore` reading (BALE.md §6.4) threaded through the
pack filter chain and the apply-time path-safety check (BALE.md §11
rule 14), the wizard's previously-deferred "anything to exclude"
prompt (now seeded with a preview of any persisted .baleignore so
the user sees what's already filtered before adding session-only
patterns), the §7.4 soft-cap `[e] edit excludes` branch (collect
more patterns, rebuild matcher, re-walk), a `--exclude` CLI flag
parallel to `--include`, and a `bale config init` step that walks
the user through `.baleignore` line-by-line (canonical persistence
surface, paired with the session-only wizard prompts above). The
remaining v0.1 item is release-tarball packaging.

Per BALE.md section 13, the v0.0.x line implements just enough to
apply its own response tarballs, plus the configurables wizard that
successive bale-on-bale sessions evolve:

    bale pack <goal> --include <paths>
    bale apply <tarball>
    bale revert <sid>
    bale retry <tarball>
    bale unlock
    bale handoff <bailout-tarball>
    bale config init

No rollback, no release-tarball packaging. Stdlib only — which since
session 003 means Python 3.11+ (tomllib lives there, inside
`bale_config`). Designed to be replaced by a v0.1 tarball that
fleshes out the full pipeline.

Sections:
   1. Imports + constants                              (~line  130)
   2. Logging                                          (~line  207)
   3. Shell / git helpers                              (~line  294)
   4. Hashing                                          (~line  333)
   5. Session IDs and the per-day counter              (~line  349)
   6. Lock handling                                    (~line  407)
   7. .gitignore handling for the .bale/ directory     (~line  438)
   8. Path-safety checks                               (~line  468)
   9. Editor invocation                                (~line  516)
  10. Pack: file enumeration and filtering             (~line  577)
  11. Pack: scope projection + threshold caps (BALE.md section 7.4) (~line  954)
  12. Pack: slug validation                            (~line 1237)
  13. Pack: manifest and tarball construction          (~line 1250)
  14. Pack: wizard                                     (~line 1365)
  15. Pack                                             (~line 1607)
  16. Apply: helpers                                   (~line 2147)
  17. Apply: pipeline                                  (~line 3168)
  18. Apply                                            (~line 3456)
  19. Revert                                           (~line 3505)
  20. Retry                                            (~line 3687)
  21. Unlock                                           (~line 3736)
  22. Handoff                                          (~line 3830)
  23. Hook invocation                                  (~line 4237)
  24. CLI                                              (~line 4360)

Configurables (loader/merger + wizard) live in the sibling
`bale_config.py` module; sections that ran in this file at v0.0.3
("bale.toml — configurables" and "`bale config init` — the
configurables wizard") moved there entire. The two remaining surfaces
that touch configurables — `run_hook` (section 23) and the `config
